WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.578
Something broke in our vault?

00:00:02.678 --> 00:00:04.292
Every one of these is common.

00:00:04.392 --> 00:00:08.430
Stalls, garbage, orphans, too big.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.821
A stalled vault is almost always capture.

00:00:12.871 --> 00:00:16.785
Summaries of summaries come from a contract that says summarise.

00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:22.812
Hand written pages get marked human. Ingest reads index dot M D first.

00:00:23.362 --> 00:00:26.248
Neither is a reason to start over with a different tool.

00:00:26.798 --> 00:00:32.370
Bad pages? Check the source. Then Claude dot M D.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:36.620
Add one good example, not another rule. Then roll back.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.150
Do not patch the bad pages by hand.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.424
Typos and renames get fixed, safe to automate.

00:00:43.474 --> 00:00:47.794
Genuine gaps go into index dot M D, never an empty page.

00:00:48.344 --> 00:00:55.859
Too big? It is retrieval economy, not disk. Summary layers. Splitting, by domain.

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:59.798
Archiving cold material. Or rebuild the index.

00:01:00.348 --> 00:01:06.546
That's chapter ten, troubleshooting. Start with page one: The failures everyone hits.
